.\"	$GergiOS$
.Dd July 11, 2026
.Dt IRQTOP 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm irqtop
.Nd display per-IRQ thread statistics
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d Ar delay
.Op Fl h
.Op Fl m Ar warn_max
.Op Fl n
.Op Fl u
.Op Fl C Ar mhz
.Op Fl H
.Op Fl s Ar col
.Op Fl r
.Op Fl i Ar irq
.Op Fl t Ar threshold
.Op Fl o Ar fmt
.Op Fl l Ar file
.Op Fl p
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
displays real-time statistics for per-IRQ kernel threads.
Each IRQ vector is serviced by a dedicated ring 0 kernel thread
running at SCHED_FIFO priority.
Statistics are read from the kernel via
.Xr sys_getinfo 2
with
.Dv GET_IRQTHREAD_STATS .
.Pp
Latency is measured as the number of TSC (Time-Stamp Counter) ticks
between the moment the kernel signals the IRQ thread and the moment
the thread begins executing the handler.
Use the
.Fl u
flag to convert latencies to nanoseconds (requires CPU MHz detection
or manual specification via
.Fl C ) .
.Pp
The columns are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width "MAX_LAT"
.It IRQ
IRQ vector number (0\(en63).
.It NAME
Short descriptive name for the IRQ (timer, keyboard, serial, msix-N, ...).
.It PRIO
SCHED_FIFO real-time priority (1\(en99, higher = more urgent).
.It CPU
CPU affinity (always 0 on uniprocessor systems).
.It HANDLED
Total number of IRQ events handled.
.It RUN
Total number of times the handler was invoked.
.It LAST_LAT / LAST_NS
Latency of the most recent handler invocation.
.It AVG_LAT / AVG_NS
Average latency over all invocations.
.It MAX_LAT / MAX_NS
Worst-case (maximum) latency observed.
.It REG
Whether an IRQ handler has been registered for this vector.
.It P50 / P95 / P99
Rolling latency percentiles (requires
.Fl H ) .
.El
.Pp
Latency values are color-coded:
.Bl -dash -offset indent
.It
Green: low latency (below ~1000 TSC ticks)
.It
Yellow: moderate latency (1000\(en10000 TSC ticks)
.It
Red: high latency (above ~10000 TSC ticks)
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl d Ar delay
Set the refresh interval in seconds (default: 1.0).
.It Fl h
Display help text and exit.
.It Fl m Ar warn_max
Highlight rows whose MAX_LAT exceeds
.Ar warn_max
TSC ticks.
Also used as the peak detection threshold with
.Fl p .
.It Fl n
One-shot mode: print statistics once and exit without clearing the screen.
Useful for scripting or non-interactive use.
.It Fl u
Show latency in nanoseconds instead of TSC ticks.
Requires CPU frequency for accurate conversion.
Use
.Fl C
to specify manually, or the CPU MHz is auto-detected from sysctl or
.Pa /proc/cpuinfo .
.It Fl C Ar mhz
Manually specify the CPU frequency in MHz for TSC to nanoseconds
conversion (used with
.Fl u ) .
.It Fl H
Enable rolling latency history columns (P50, P95, P99).
Tracks up to 120 samples per IRQ in a circular buffer and displays
percentile statistics for each IRQ.
.It Fl s Ar col
Sort the table by column.
Valid columns are:
.Bl -tag -width "name, prio" -compact
.It irq
By IRQ number (default)
.It lat
By max latency descending
.It hits
By handled count descending
.It name
Alphabetically by IRQ name
.It prio
By RT priority descending
.El
.It Fl r
Show only registered IRQs (hide inactive slots).
.It Fl i Ar irq
Show only the specified IRQ vector (e.g.,
.Fl i 4
for serial1).
.It Fl t Ar threshold
Show only IRQs whose MAX_LAT exceeds the given threshold.
.It Fl o Ar fmt
Output format.
Valid formats are:
.Bl -tag -width "json, csv" -compact
.It table
Default formatted table (ANSI colors on supporting terminals)
.It json
JSON object with all IRQ statistics
.It csv
Comma-separated values with header row
.El
.It Fl l Ar file
Log snapshot data to a file in CSV format.
Each poll cycle appends one row per IRQ.
The file is created if it does not exist, and a header is written
on first write.
.It Fl p
Peak detection mode.
Only log IRQs whose MAX_LAT exceeds the warning threshold
.Pq Fl m
to the log file.
Defaults to
.Pa /var/log/irqtop.peaks .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag
.It Nm
Display statistics with a 1-second refresh.
.It Nm Fl d 0.5 Fl m 10000
Refresh every 500 ms, highlight IRQs with more than 10,000 ticks latency.
.It Nm Fl n
Print a single snapshot to stdout.
.It Nm Fl s lat Fl r
Sort by max latency, show only registered IRQs.
.It Nm Fl u Fl C 2400
Show latency in nanoseconds, specify 2.4 GHz CPU.
.It Nm Fl H
Enable rolling history with percentile columns.
.It Nm Fl o json
Output a single snapshot as JSON.
.It Nm Fl l /var/log/irq.log
Log snapshots to a file in the background.
.It Nm Fl p Fl m 5000
Peak detection: log only when MAX_LAT exceeds 5000 ticks.
.It Nm Fl i 4 Fl s hits
Show only IRQ 4 (serial1), sorted by handled count.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr top 1 ,
.Xr systat 1 ,
.Xr sys_getinfo 2
.Sh AUTHORS
.An GergiOS
